# Keep SQL migrations byte-identical and host-independent so sqlx::migrate!
# compile-time checksums stay stable across machines (LF everywhere). The
# committed (index) form of every migration is already LF; this pins the
# working-tree form to LF too. Path-agnostic on purpose: the migrations dir
# moves under the lumina workspace carve (lumina/migrations -> later
# lumina/core/migrations), so a fixed path would go stale.
*.sql text eol=lf

# Pin Rust sources to LF in the working tree as well. core.autocrlf is true, so
# a checkout would otherwise write CRLF while rustfmt rewrites the files it
# touches as LF -- leaving the tree mixed and making every later git command
# over the crate print a line-ending warning per file. The index is already LF
# throughout, so this changes no committed content; the CRLF files still on
# disk convert on their next checkout.
*.rs text eol=lf

# Pin the flow agent definitions to LF. Two of them carry the shared blocks
# scripts/verify-shared-blocks.sh holds byte-identical, and its awk matches the
# markers by whole-line equality -- under a CR-preserving awk (the mandated
# gawk strips it) both blocks extract empty and the empty-block guard fails
# every commit. Directory-scoped so a later agent carrier is covered too.
# Nothing committed changes: both extractors strip the CR before hashing, so
# the block hashes are unaffected and the files convert on their next checkout.
claude/agents/*.md text eol=lf
